[b][size=6]SkTestLab — Skript Testing & Diagnostics for VS Code[/size][/b]

Write Skript, check it in Test Explorer, and inspect the evidence behind every result.

[b]Free · MIT open source · Version 1.0.0 · Windows x64[/b]

[b][size=5]Features[/size][/b]
[list]
[*]Source diagnostics and targeted Quick Fixes.
[*]Offline tests for diagnostics, symbols, source and structure.
[*]Real runtime assertions using your own Paper and Skript JARs in a disposable environment.
[*]Native Test Explorer, cancellation, rerun failed tests and saved run history.
[*]White, Dark and Follow VS Code dashboard themes, assertion details, filters, sorting and comparable-run trends.
[*]JSON, HTML and JUnit report exports.
[*]Portable Reward Lab example with seven runtime assertions. No account or telemetry required.
[/list]

[b][size=5]Requirements[/size][/b]
Windows x64 and VS Code 1.96+. Offline tests require no Minecraft server or Java.

Runtime tests require a trusted workspace, a suitable Java version, your own compatible Paper/Skript JARs and your acceptance of the Minecraft EULA. No server/plugin JARs or preaccepted EULA settings are distributed.

Minecraft 1.21+ is the compatibility target with a matching Skript release. Verified pairings are Paper 1.21 build 130 / Skript 2.9.0 and Paper 1.21.11 build 132 / Skript 2.14.0 or 2.16.0, using Java 21.0.12. Other pairings and addons need local verification. Linux, macOS and Windows ARM64 are not certified.

[b][size=5]First test[/size][/b]
[list=1]
[*]Extract the download ZIP and install its VSIX through Extensions → … → Install from VSIX. This is an editor extension, not a Minecraft plugin.
[*]Extract reward-lab.zip and open its reward-lab folder in VS Code.
[*]Run the offline test in Testing. Use SkTestLab: Open Dashboard to inspect the result.
[*]Use SkTestLab: Configure Runtime for actual Paper execution, then run the reward runtime test.
[/list]
The included INSTALL.md and TESTING-GUIDE.md provide the full walkthrough.

[b][size=5]Scope[/size][/b]
Offline analysis uses structural heuristics rather than a complete Skript parser. Runtime tests use console context and exported functions. Automated players, arbitrary event simulation, debugging and coverage are outside this release. Temporary environments prevent accidental production-world reuse; they are not an OS security sandbox. Skipped, errored and cancelled tests do not count as passed.

